---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';

// TODO before launch: add the operating legal entity, its registered address and,
// if required in your jurisdiction, a data protection contact. Have a lawyer review.
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy notice — KAVOVO"
  description="What data KAVOVO collects, why, and how to have it removed."
>
  <TextPage
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy notice"
    intro="A short, honest description of what happens to data when you visit KAVOVO."
    updated="2026-08-05"
  >
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      KAVOVO is a static website. We do not run advertising, we do not set tracking cookies, and we do not sell or share
      personal data. The only personal data we deliberately collect is an email address, and only if you hand it to us.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Nothing, if you only read.</strong> Browsing recipes and guides requires no account and sets no cookies
        from us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your email address,</strong> if you subscribe to the newsletter or join the shop waitlist. We store the
        address, the date, and which form you used, so we can send the right emails and prove consent.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data — including IP
      address, browser type and requested URL — to deliver pages and protect against abuse. We do not use that data to
      build profiles of visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use PostHog, hosted in the EU, for anonymous product analytics. It tells us which parts of the Brew Assistant
      people use and where they stop — nothing about who they are.
    </p>
    <p>
      It runs without cookies and without building a profile of you. We have turned off automatic click tracking,
      session recording and person profiles, so events are only sent at the specific points we have chosen.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is sent: which brewing method was chosen, which symptom was reported, which recommendation the assistant
      gave, whether you marked it helpful, and which article you opened next.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is never sent: your coffee dose, water, brew time or temperature, anything you typed, the identifier of a
      brew saved in your browser, or your email address. Your brew history stays in your own browser and is never
      uploaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you block analytics with a browser extension or a content blocker, the Brew Assistant carries on working
      exactly as before.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      The newsletter is not yet running. When it launches, subscriptions will use double opt-in: you enter your address,
      we email you a confirmation link, and nothing is sent until you click it. Every email will carry a one-click
      unsubscribe link, and unsubscribing removes your address from the sending list.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email we send.</li>
      <li>
        Ask us what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be deleted, by emailing
        <a href="mailto:hello@kavovo.coffee">hello@kavovo.coffee</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to answer requests within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this notice changes we update the date at the top. Material changes to how we handle email addresses will
      also be announced in the newsletter itself.
    </p>
  </TextPage>
</Layout>
